{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FJY2uEfJwJTbe697Cuqunq","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines scoring criteria acceptance rate\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"2025 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Survey - Speaker Deck\",\"url\":\"https://speakerdeck.com/harukiabe/corl-2025-survey\"},{\"title\":\"What Drives Paper Acceptance? A Process-Centric Analysis of Modern Peer Review\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.25701\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2024-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"The AI Review Lottery: Widespread AI-Assisted Peer Reviews Boost Paper   Scores and Acceptance Rates\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2405.02150\"},{\"title\":\"Best Reviewers Award for 2024\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11955497/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some information related to reviewer guidelines, but the results primarily returned information about NeurIPS 2025 and CoRL 2023 rather than specific CoRL 2025 guidelines.\n\nHere's what I found:\n\n**CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines:**\nCoRL builds its reviewer guidelines on ICML and NeurIPS resources to provide guidance on writing constructive reviews. The CoRL review process is about three months long, submission-to-notification, including the discussion period.\n\n**Scoring Criteria:**\nThe search results don't contain specific scoring criteria details for CoRL 2025. However, the NeurIPS 2025 results show they use a scale that includes options like \"6: Strong Accept\" for technically flawless papers with groundbreaking impact.\n\n**Acceptance Rate:**\nThe search results do not include specific acceptance rate information for CoRL 2025. CoRL 2025 overview mentions participation scale and acceptance information, but the detailed numbers are not provided in these results.\n\nTo get the most current and complete CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines, scoring criteria, and acceptance rate, I'd recommend checking the official CoRL 2025 website directly, as the search results appear to be primarily from previous years or related conferences.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24463d9a-eaaf-4e5b-b633-10caf5e13734","uuid":"623e5c84-5b83-4b16-966e-de22ef03f44c","timestamp":"2026-05-20T16:47:51.667Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines scoring criteria acceptance rate","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_016DSBhQ5hiRc4m3kMyBJN57","content":[{"title":"2025 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Survey - Speaker Deck","url":"https://speakerdeck.com/harukiabe/corl-2025-survey"},{"title":"What Drives Paper Acceptance? A Process-Centric Analysis of Modern Peer Review","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.25701"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2024-paper-list/"},{"title":"The AI Review Lottery: Widespread AI-Assisted Peer Reviews Boost Paper   Scores and Acceptance Rates","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2405.02150"},{"title":"Best Reviewers Award for 2024","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11955497/"}]},"Based on the search results, I found some information related to reviewer guidelines, but the results primarily returned information about NeurIPS 2025 and CoRL 2023 rather than specific CoRL 2025 guidelines.\n\nHere's what I found:\n\n**CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines:**\nCoRL builds its reviewer guidelines on ICML and NeurIPS resources to provide guidance on writing constructive reviews. The CoRL review process is about three months long, submission-to-notification, including the discussion period.\n\n**Scoring Criteria:**\nThe search results don't contain specific scoring criteria details for CoRL 2025. However, the NeurIPS 2025 results show they use a scale that includes options like \"6: Strong Accept\" for technically flawless papers with groundbreaking impact.\n\n**Acceptance Rate:**\nThe search results do not include specific acceptance rate information for CoRL 2025. CoRL 2025 overview mentions participation scale and acceptance information, but the detailed numbers are not provided in these results.\n\nTo get the most current and complete CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines, scoring criteria, and acceptance rate, I'd recommend checking the official CoRL 2025 website directly, as the search results appear to be primarily from previous years or related conferences."],"durationSeconds":5.837859128}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LwAgUJf5JQRhrHtAWp3FcM","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found information about CoRL 2026, though specific dedicated reviewer guidelines and review form documents for 2026 were not directly available in the search results. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Information\n\nCoRL 2026 will be held November 9-12, 2026 in Austin, Texas, US, and it is an annual international conference focusing on the intersection of robotics and machine learning.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer, and they are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ ICRA/ IROS/ RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/ NeurIPS/ ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\n## Review Process\n\nCoRL aims to have at least two reviewers per paper. Additionally, the accepted papers and reviews will be publicly accessible and de-anonymized after decisions are announced.\n\nFor more specific information about the CoRL 2026 review form and detailed reviewer guidelines, you may want to check the official CoRL 2026 OpenReview page at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference or contact the conference organizers directly through the CoRL website.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24463d9a-eaaf-4e5b-b633-10caf5e13734","uuid":"d2b45b68-68ef-4a64-91f0-484a73f6c0ce","timestamp":"2026-05-20T16:47:51.705Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_0162r8uCHiX4CGFq2RwxjYJt","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"}]},"Based on the web search results, I found information about CoRL 2026, though specific dedicated reviewer guidelines and review form documents for 2026 were not directly available in the search results. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Information\n\nCoRL 2026 will be held November 9-12, 2026 in Austin, Texas, US, and it is an annual international conference focusing on the intersection of robotics and machine learning.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer, and they are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ ICRA/ IROS/ RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/ NeurIPS/ ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\n## Review Process\n\nCoRL aims to have at least two reviewers per paper. Additionally, the accepted papers and reviews will be publicly accessible and de-anonymized after decisions are announced.\n\nFor more specific information about the CoRL 2026 review form and detailed reviewer guidelines, you may want to check the official CoRL 2026 OpenReview page at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference or contact the conference organizers directly through the CoRL website."],"durationSeconds":6.027381683}}
