rmance), reduces in Cheetah (σ=0.5, NVE from 8-108× to 1.5-4×).\n\nExperiments: 4 DMC environments (Walker Walk, Cheetah Run, Cartpole Swingup, Hopper Hop), 30+ configurations, 60+ seeds.\n\n## Related Work as Presented in the Paper (Section 2)\nThe paper covers:\n- **Temporal abstraction in RL:** Options framework [Sutton et al. 1999; Precup 2000], FiGAR [Sharma et al. 2017], action repeat [Lakshminarayanan et al. 2017]\n- **World-model RL:** Dreamer family [Hafner et al. 2020, 2021, 2023], IRIS [Micheli et al. 2023], TWM [Robine et al. 2023]\n- **Variable-rate planning:** TAWM [Nhu et al. ICML 2025] — key contrast paper (MPC vs imagination-based)\n- **Value overestimation in MBRL:** Model exploitation [Janner et al. 2019], delusional bias [Lu et al. 2018]\n- Also cites: THICK [Kim et al. 2024], Hieros [Robine et al. ICML 2024] in discussion\n\nTotal references: 17\n\n## Your Task (R2: Novelty + Related Work)\n\nEvaluate the following dimensions thoroughly:\n\n### 1. Novelty Assessment\n- Is CIVO a genuinely new phenomenon, or a known failure mode (model exploitation / value overestimation in MBRL) applied to a specific setting?\n- How novel is the diagnosis (NVE metric)? Is it just a normalized V/E ratio — a standard diagnostic?\n- How novel is TCN (noise injection during imagination)? Noise injection for regularization is a well-known technique (dropout, label smoothing, noisy nets, etc.). Is applying it to dt_embedding truly novel?\n- Is the dual-pathway (A vs B) distinction a genuine conceptual contribution or an empirical observation?\n- The forward-pass vs backward-pass distinction — is this a methodological insight or just a negative result?\n\n### 2. Related Work Completeness\n- Only 17 references — is this sufficient for a venue like CoRL?\n- Missing important related work? Consider:\n  - Value overestimation literature beyond MBRL: TD3 [Fujimoto et al. 2018], REDQ, etc.\n  - Model regularization in MBRL: PETS, MBPO, conservative model exploitation\n  - Temporal abstraction beyond options: HAM, MAXQ, skill discovery\n  - Other world model architectures with temporal conditioning\n  - Noise injection as regularization: broader ML literature\n  - DreamerV3 analysis/failure mode papers\n  - Semi-MDP / variable timestep literature in control\n- Is the TAWM comparison fair and complete? The paper argues MPC re-plans from real states while imagination bootstraps — is this the complete picture?\n\n### 3. Positioning and Framing\n- Is the paper positioned correctly? It studies DreamerV3 on DMC — is this more of a \"negative result / empirical analysis\" paper or a \"method\" paper?\n- The title says \"Diagnosing and Mitigating\" — but TCN is only partially effective (Cheetah NVE still 1.5-4×). Is the framing honest?\n- All claims scoped to DreamerV3 + RSSM — how limited is this? Would findings transfer to other world models?\n- For CoRL: the paper has no robotics component. Is \"DreamerV3 failure mode analysis on DMC\" relevant enough?\n\n### 4. Intellectual Contribution\n- What is the lasting insight? If DreamerV3 is superseded (THICK, Hieros, transformer world models), does this analysis remain relevant?\n- Is the paper's contribution primarily empirical (lots of experiments showing something breaks) or conceptual (a transferable insight about temporal conditioning in world models)?\n- The \"forward-pass vs backward-pass\" framing — does this generalize beyond this specific setting?\n\n### 5. Writing and Presentation\n- Is the paper well-written? Is the narrative clear?\n- Are the 8 claims well-organized or is there claim inflation?\n- Is the paper too long / too detailed for the amount of conceptual novelty?\n\n## Output Format\n\nProvide your review in this exact structure:\n\n```\n## R2 Review: Novelty and Related Work\n\n### Summary\n[2-3 sentence summary from your perspective]\n\n### Strengths\n[Numbered list, each with a short bold title and 1-2 sentence explanation]\n\n### Weaknesses\n[Numbered list, each with a short bold title and 1-2 sentence explanation]\n\n### Questions for Authors\n[Numbered list of specific questions]\n\n### Missing Related Work\n[Specific papers or research directions that should be cited and discussed]\n\n### Novelty Assessment\n- CIVO phenomenon: [High/Medium/Low] novelty — [brief justification]\n- NVE diagnostic: [High/Medium/Low] novelty\n- TCN mitigation: [High/Medium/Low] novelty\n- Forward-pass vs backward-pass insight: [High/Medium/Low] novelty\n- Dual-pathway distinction: [High/Medium/Low] novelty\n- Overall novelty: [High/Medium/Low]\n\n### Scores\n- Novelty: [1-4] (1=incremental, 4=groundbreaking)\n- Related Work: [1-4] (1=major gaps, 4=comprehensive)\n- Clarity: [1-4]\n- Significance: [1-4]\n- CoRL Relevance: [1-4]\n- Overall Rating: [1-10, CoRL scale]\n- Confidence: [1-5]\n```\n","uuid":"5916d72c-56a4-4261-89b6-69c3eaed0c4d","session_id":"24463d9a-eaaf-4e5b-b633-10caf5e13734"}
